(106328, 4565, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background5,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,<br/>Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 4,<br/>Total Averaged Rating6.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background5,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 4,Total Averaged Rating6.   Autool', '2002-08-22 10:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106329, 4565, 2123, '<td valign="top">Wow, what great colors!  Looks like a lot of thought went into this layout</td>', 'Wow, what great colors!  Looks like a lot of thought went into this layout', '2002-08-22 16:08:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106330, 4565, 436, '<td valign="top">How about a sheet as a background?  What if instead of the exacting symmetry of the layout, it was a bit more random...or lead my eye to the large pencil in a different arrangement?  I like the variety of pencils and the color choices you made.  It just lacks that POW! to make it an exceptional photo.  This will be a good week to more closely examine the very graphic submissions.  A lot of people tried similiar techniques, only a few very successfully.  5</td>', 'How about a sheet as a background?  What if instead of the exacting symmetry of the layout, it was a bit more random...or lead my eye to the large pencil in a different arrangement?  I like the variety of pencils and the color choices you made.  It just lacks that POW! to make it an exceptional photo.  This will be a good week to more closely examine the very graphic submissions.  A lot of people tried similiar techniques, only a few very successfully.  5', '2002-08-23 15:12:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106331, 4565, 2302, '<td valign="top">I appreciate the time taken to make this design - but the picture ends up being very flat when taken from above the pencils. If you could have made the design so the pencils were standing up (or maybe if they were all leaning against the big pencil in the middle? - and then taken the picture at an even level with them I think it would be more appealing. The lighting is good and your focus is good too = 5</td>', 'I appreciate the time taken to make this design - but the picture ends up being very flat when taken from above the pencils. If you could have made the design so the pencils were standing up (or maybe if they were all leaning against the big pencil in the middle? - and then taken the picture at an even level with them I think it would be more appealing. The lighting is good and your focus is good too = 5', '2002-08-23 15:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106332, 4565, 1808, '<td valign="top">That must be one BIG pencil in the middle.</td>', 'That must be one BIG pencil in the middle.', '2002-08-25 18:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106333, 4566, 2928, '<td valign="top">Technically well done, meets the challenge.</td>', 'Technically well done, meets the challenge.', '2002-08-19 06:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106334, 4566, 889, '<td valign="top">interesting use of different colored lights</td>', 'interesting use of different colored lights', '2002-08-19 13:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106335, 4566, 2152, '<td valign="top">I think if you found some way to eliminate the shadows, possibly by moving the clamp a few feet from the background, this shot would have more of an impact.  Also, it looks like the clamp and the pencil are both a little underexposed.</td>', 'I think if you found some way to eliminate the shadows, possibly by moving the clamp a few feet from the background, this shot would have more of an impact.  Also, it looks like the clamp and the pencil are both a little underexposed.', '2002-08-20 13:06:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106336, 4566, 3080, '<td valign="top">It took me a minute to figure this out.  It''s really neat.  Lighting and angle are good.  I like how it fits in the frame.  Very clever and unique.  Another idea is to use a carpenters pencil.  I think it would look cool that way too.  I like the simplicity of this.  It''s not too busy and it''s a neat balance.  You did a nice job of getting in close on this.  Don''t know if too many people will realize it''s only a 2" c clamp.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'It took me a minute to figure this out.  It''s really neat.  Lighting and angle are good.  I like how it fits in the frame.  Very clever and unique.  Another idea is to use a carpenters pencil.  I think it would look cool that way too.  I like the simplicity of this.  It''s not too busy and it''s a neat balance.  You did a nice job of getting in close on this.  Don''t know if too many people will realize it''s only a 2" c clamp.  Great job and good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-20 18:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106337, 4566, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,<br/>Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 4,<br/>Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background7,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 4,Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool', '2002-08-20 20:11:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106338, 4566, 2172, '<td valign="top">Very creative idea.  IMO (not to offend) I think this would''ve been better with diff lighting.  I''m going to assume that the the grey background was not itentional.  I suggest manipulating the white balance on the camera or tweaking the gamma in PS.  I say this because when I satarted, I didn''t even realize how grey the white was.  It also appears to me that the point of focus is on the eraser - where as I would have chosen the point of the pencil.  One last thing, I would''ve prefered to be able to see the details a little more on the screw.  I''m in the process of learning about how to manipulate light myself - (boy I need practice), but I think I''m slowly catching on.  I do like the composition and the idea...ooh just thought of something - would''ve been more effective if the pencil appeared to be jumping out/reaching out - I can almost sense that was possible the intention - to me, like I mentioned earlier, would focus on the pencil and use a medium dof - only to slightly blur the back - creating that reaching out effect.  I''m in no a way an expert and only giving you my take on this.  I still recognize the effort and time put into this.  Great job!  5<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Very creative idea.  IMO (not to offend) I think this would''ve been better with diff lighting.  I''m going to assume that the the grey background was not itentional.  I suggest manipulating the white balance on the camera or tweaking the gamma in PS.  I say this because when I satarted, I didn''t even realize how grey the white was.  It also appears to me that the point of focus is on the eraser - where as I would have chosen the point of the pencil.  One last thing, I would''ve prefered to be able to see the details a little more on the screw.  I''m in the process of learning about how to manipulate light myself - (boy I need practice), but I think I''m slowly catching on.  I do like the composition and the idea...ooh just thought of something - would''ve been more effective if the pencil appeared to be jumping out/reaching out - I can almost sense that was possible the intention - to me, like I mentioned earlier, would focus on the pencil and use a medium dof - only to slightly blur the back - creating that reaching out effect.  I''m in no a way an expert and only giving you my take on this.  I still recognize the effort and time put into this.  Great job!  5Ruthann', '2002-08-21 14:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106339, 4566, 772, '<td valign="top">Nicely done photo and excellent depth of field :)  = 7 - jmsetzler</td>', 'Nicely done photo and excellent depth of field :)  = 7 - jmsetzler', '2002-08-21 14:28:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106340, 4566, 3087, '<td valign="top">Like the weird angles and the lighting, and the simplicity of contents. <br/>6, Kavey</td>', 'Like the weird angles and the lighting, and the simplicity of contents. 6, Kavey', '2002-08-21 19:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106341, 4566, 1280, '<td valign="top">From my perspective:<br/>Meets challenge:Yes<br/>Technical:Well done<br/>Appeal/Artistic:Ok<br/>Composition:Very good.  Strong lines, uncluttered, good background<br/>Originality:Excellent.  I don''t think the average person would have thought this up. A simple union of two unrelated objects. The yellow pencil stands out among the mostly black and white image.<br/>Comments:Good job.  Good luck in the challenge.<br/></td>', 'From my perspective:Meets challenge:YesTechnical:Well doneAppeal/Artistic:OkComposition:Very good.  Strong lines, uncluttered, good backgroundOriginality:Excellent.  I don''t think the average person would have thought this up. A simple union of two unrelated objects. The yellow pencil stands out among the mostly black and white image.Comments:Good job.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-21 20:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106342, 4566, 2752, '<td valign="top">the pencil as good perspective</td>', 'the pencil as good perspective', '2002-08-22 00:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106343, 4566, 2667, '<td valign="top">i like the clean lines and strong angles. very nice. (6) ~mcmurma</td>', 'i like the clean lines and strong angles. very nice. (6) ~mcmurma', '2002-08-22 03:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106344, 4566, 715, '<td valign="top">Great idea, but most of the attention is drawn to the clamp itself though, not to the real point of interest. I think this could have been achieved by shifting everything downwards even though it would have cut off part of the clamp. Somehow, I also would like to see the pencil being really squeezed.</td>', 'Great idea, but most of the attention is drawn to the clamp itself though, not to the real point of interest. I think this could have been achieved by shifting everything downwards even though it would have cut off part of the clamp. Somehow, I also would like to see the pencil being really squeezed.', '2002-08-22 17:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106345, 4566, 3189, '<td valign="top">Interesting idea, I like, but I think a shallower DoF would have made it more catching.</td>', 'Interesting idea, I like, but I think a shallower DoF would have made it more catching.', '2002-08-23 18:05:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106346, 4567, 1827, '<td valign="top">Ha.  Nicely executed.  The B/W choice was a good one for this photo.   Yellow would have detracted from your point, er, should I say, your purpose.  8</td>', 'Ha.  Nicely executed.  The B/W choice was a good one for this photo.   Yellow would have detracted from your point, er, should I say, your purpose.  8', '2002-08-19 03:49:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106347, 4567, 2120, '<td valign="top">Well, I am not finished voting yet but this is the best picture so far. I can''t identify what is sticking out above the P on ther pencil, but I can''t help wondering if it could be done away with. It is the only distraction I see from an otherwise dare I say ''perfect'' shot. This might be one to retake and attempt to publish somewhere. <br/>--10 Agamemnon   (I really like this)</td>', 'Well, I am not finished voting yet but this is the best picture so far. I can''t identify what is sticking out above the P on ther pencil, but I can''t help wondering if it could be done away with. It is the only distraction I see from an otherwise dare I say ''perfect'' shot. This might be one to retake and attempt to publish somewhere. --10 Agamemnon   (I really like this)', '2002-08-19 08:48:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106348, 4567, 3280, '<td valign="top">Great idea, very creative.</td>', 'Great idea, very creative.', '2002-08-19 10:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106349, 4567, 3080, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful.  One of 6 10''s this week.  Black and white is awesome.  I think that if it had been in color, it would have taken away from the "likeness" of the pencil to the tree.  Yes, I like the background being oof.  Is that an ant making it''s self at home on your pencil?  Alternate title could be "like father like son". lol.  Great lighting, great angle, focus, appeal.  Excelent shot and good luck with the challenge.</td>', 'This is beautiful.  One of 6 10''s this week.  Black and white is awesome.  I think that if it had been in color, it would have taken away from the "likeness" of the pencil to the tree.  Yes, I like the background being oof.  Is that an ant making it''s self at home on your pencil?  Alternate title could be "like father like son". lol.  Great lighting, great angle, focus, appeal.  Excelent shot and good luck with the challenge.', '2002-08-19 11:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106350, 4567, 2897, '<td valign="top">this picture made me smile!  Very nice idea!</td>', 'this picture made me smile!  Very nice idea!', '2002-08-19 11:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
