(106788, 4599, 436, '<td valign="top">a touch more visible texture to the paper on top or less sharpening, maybe?  that area seems a bit too stark to me.  It''s an extraordinary drawing and a very nice arrangement.</td>', 'a touch more visible texture to the paper on top or less sharpening, maybe?  that area seems a bit too stark to me.  It''s an extraordinary drawing and a very nice arrangement.', '2002-08-23 15:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106789, 4599, 3251, '<td valign="top">This is easily the best of the "pencil while drawing" shots. I''m not sure about originality because so many had the same idea, but technically it''s superior.</td>', 'This is easily the best of the "pencil while drawing" shots. I''m not sure about originality because so many had the same idea, but technically it''s superior.', '2002-08-24 02:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106790, 4599, 3352, '<td valign="top">very cleaver</td>', 'very cleaver', '2002-08-25 14:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106791, 4599, 1808, '<td valign="top">Clever picture of a drawing!</td>', 'Clever picture of a drawing!', '2002-08-25 17:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106792, 4599, 1128, '<td valign="top">This is very clever, and I think it would be even more clever if there was no hand and the pencil was (by itself) drawing a self portrait.  Did you draw the picture on the paper, or was it a photoshop job?</td>', 'This is very clever, and I think it would be even more clever if there was no hand and the pencil was (by itself) drawing a self portrait.  Did you draw the picture on the paper, or was it a photoshop job?', '2002-08-25 23:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106793, 4599, 1847, '<td valign="top">Nice drawing.  Neat concept.  Would have liked to have NOT seen the wall or whatever in the lower left.</td>', 'Nice drawing.  Neat concept.  Would have liked to have NOT seen the wall or whatever in the lower left.', '2002-08-26 00:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106794, 4599, 2003, '<td valign="top">Drawing is actually a photo of a pencil tweaked in PS, hand is mine - couldn''t get rid of that paper edge without blowing out the rest of the pic, but i kinda liked it (apparently quite a few did not :(</td>', 'Drawing is actually a photo of a pencil tweaked in PS, hand is mine - couldn''t get rid of that paper edge without blowing out the rest of the pic, but i kinda liked it (apparently quite a few did not :(', '2002-08-26 01:56:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(106795, 4600, 1827, '<td valign="top">I think the framing would have been more interesting is the box were rotated on a slight diagonal and the crayons were lots all lined up precisely.  5</td>', 'I think the framing would have been more interesting is the box were rotated on a slight diagonal and the crayons were lots all lined up precisely.  5', '2002-08-19 02:29:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106796, 4600, 3239, '<td valign="top">It''s a bit dark, I think the lighting could have been a bit better.  Overall not bad.</td>', 'It''s a bit dark, I think the lighting could have been a bit better.  Overall not bad.', '2002-08-19 15:22:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106797, 4600, 2867, '<td valign="top">perhaps a more interesting angle would''ve made this photo seem more appealing, good idea though</td>', 'perhaps a more interesting angle would''ve made this photo seem more appealing, good idea though', '2002-08-19 18:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106798, 4600, 2334, '<td valign="top">haha</td>', 'haha', '2002-08-19 19:17:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106799, 4600, 2279, '<td valign="top">The centering and angle of this picture don''t really do anything for me. A few degrees to the left or right might help a bit. 5.</td>', 'The centering and angle of this picture don''t really do anything for me. A few degrees to the left or right might help a bit. 5.', '2002-08-20 01:37:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106800, 4600, 2798, '<td valign="top">Great idea! Not sure this was the most interesting angle you could have taken the photo from. Nice clean background though. I would suggest cropping in closer but I see that your camera''s resolution would start giving you problems if you did.</td>', 'Great idea! Not sure this was the most interesting angle you could have taken the photo from. Nice clean background though. I would suggest cropping in closer but I see that your camera''s resolution would start giving you problems if you did.', '2002-08-20 08:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106801, 4600, 3087, '<td valign="top">Nice, says a lot more than just a pencil in a crayon box to me. Talks of round pegs in square holes and whether or not one should try and fit into a mould and peer pressure and lots of things. Don''t even know if that''s what was intended or it is just a pencil in a crayon box. Would score higher if was horizontal within frame.<br/>6, Kavey</td>', 'Nice, says a lot more than just a pencil in a crayon box to me. Talks of round pegs in square holes and whether or not one should try and fit into a mould and peer pressure and lots of things. Don''t even know if that''s what was intended or it is just a pencil in a crayon box. Would score higher if was horizontal within frame.6, Kavey', '2002-08-20 18:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106802, 4600, 1202, '<td valign="top">Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background6,<br/>Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,<br/>Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,<br/>Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,<br/>Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool<br/></td>', 'Composition: Subject Placement, Cropping, Background6,Technical: Focus, Exposure, Lighting, Processing5,Challenge: Does your entry meet it?10,Appeal: Is it Interesting, Motivating, Etc.? 5,Total Averaged Rating7.   Autool', '2002-08-20 20:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106803, 4600, 3002, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, but very WRONG angle (sorry).  Nice idea though, and the focus, DOF is interesting.</td>', 'Nice idea, but very WRONG angle (sorry).  Nice idea though, and the focus, DOF is interesting.', '2002-08-21 02:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106804, 4600, 2204, '<td valign="top">I think I recognize these crayons......A little fuzzy and maybe a bit dark but is a nice composition. I think the slight tilt is more of an attraction than a distraction.  I will be watching to see what other people more experienced than I will comment about that. =5 syamjonimi ;''-D</td>', 'I think I recognize these crayons......A little fuzzy and maybe a bit dark but is a nice composition. I think the slight tilt is more of an attraction than a distraction.  I will be watching to see what other people more experienced than I will comment about that. =5 syamjonimi ;''-D', '2002-08-21 03:46:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106805, 4600, 2752, '<td valign="top">I think  if the encil were pulled out a little it would have fit the title better..nice idea though.</td>', 'I think  if the encil were pulled out a little it would have fit the title better..nice idea though.', '2002-08-21 11:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106806, 4600, 3162, '<td valign="top">Good idea. Simplistic and out of the box. (or in) not sure. Feel like a pencil and crayon world myself sometimes.</td>', 'Good idea. Simplistic and out of the box. (or in) not sure. Feel like a pencil and crayon world myself sometimes.', '2002-08-21 11:42:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106807, 4600, 811, '<td valign="top">I like the perspective and focus here.  Was the slight tilt on purpose?   karmat</td>', 'I like the perspective and focus here.  Was the slight tilt on purpose?   karmat', '2002-08-21 16:09:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106808, 4600, 2172, '<td valign="top">Nice idea.  I''m being straight out - NOT to offend.  I see a few things that I would adjust.  For something like this, I would make sure that the subject was level - or if intended to be tilted, then more tilt - this looks as if that part wasn''t carefully considered.  The light source appears to be a flash - not effective for this.  Personally, I use regular household lights - no money for expensive stuff.  I would also try to balance the light evenly trying to avoid the shadows - better yet, with a lamp or something, place the light souce lower and to the side.  The background is too grey, that is, assuming it was supposed to be white.  I would adjust the white balance on the camera, if possible.  I appreciate the time and effort put into this.    I am in no way an expert.  I am still in the learning process myself.   5<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Nice idea.  I''m being straight out - NOT to offend.  I see a few things that I would adjust.  For something like this, I would make sure that the subject was level - or if intended to be tilted, then more tilt - this looks as if that part wasn''t carefully considered.  The light source appears to be a flash - not effective for this.  Personally, I use regular household lights - no money for expensive stuff.  I would also try to balance the light evenly trying to avoid the shadows - better yet, with a lamp or something, place the light souce lower and to the side.  The background is too grey, that is, assuming it was supposed to be white.  I would adjust the white balance on the camera, if possible.  I appreciate the time and effort put into this.    I am in no way an expert.  I am still in the learning process myself.   5Ruthann', '2002-08-21 21:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106809, 4600, 2158, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, but I find the composition rather uninteresting.  I would have preferred to see the box at an angle, rather than parallel to the borders.</td>', 'Nice idea, but I find the composition rather uninteresting.  I would have preferred to see the box at an angle, rather than parallel to the borders.', '2002-08-21 22:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106810, 4600, 3080, '<td valign="top">I probably shouldn''t comment on this one.  I might be bias towards head on shots of crayons coming out of the box. LOL. (in case you hadn''t seen it, I did a very similar shot in the something new challenge called "out of the box")  It was so hard for me to photograph the crayons to look clear and in focus because of 1. the shiny-ness, and 2. the wrappers on crayola crayons are textured to begin with and take on a grainy, oof look.  the lighting for this is perfect, and the background makes the crayons stand out.  definately has a pencil in it.  The only complaint I might have would be the tilt of the box. I think I would have liked to see this level with the top and bottom of the photo.  Otherwise, very nice shot.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I probably shouldn''t comment on this one.  I might be bias towards head on shots of crayons coming out of the box. LOL. (in case you hadn''t seen it, I did a very similar shot in the something new challenge called "out of the box")  It was so hard for me to photograph the crayons to look clear and in focus because of 1. the shiny-ness, and 2. the wrappers on crayola crayons are textured to begin with and take on a grainy, oof look.  the lighting for this is perfect, and the background makes the crayons stand out.  definately has a pencil in it.  The only complaint I might have would be the tilt of the box. I think I would have liked to see this level with the top and bottom of the photo.  Otherwise, very nice shot.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-23 16:10:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106811, 4600, 3500, '<td valign="top">Nice!  I would like to see the crayon box squared-up to the edge of the picture frame.</td>', 'Nice!  I would like to see the crayon box squared-up to the edge of the picture frame.', '2002-08-24 18:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(106812, 4601, 2223, '<td valign="top">uh-oh!</td>', 'uh-oh!', '2002-08-19 01:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
