(107013, 4613, 1759, '<td valign="top">Very good composition. The photo has good focus and depth of field, which is appropriate to the subject and arrangement. My personal nitpick preference would be for B&amp;W or sepia, but the yellow is a bit too strong for me.</td>', 'Very good composition. The photo has good focus and depth of field, which is appropriate to the subject and arrangement. My personal nitpick preference would be for B&W or sepia, but the yellow is a bit too strong for me.', '2002-08-21 22:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107014, 4613, 3080, '<td valign="top">This is very yellow.  I am sure you did it intentionally, so I''m going to leave it alone, however I might have either used b&amp;w or plain old fashioned color.  You did a great job in creating the yellowness, just a bit too yellow for me.  Setting that aside, You have a great angle of the child and there is definately a pencil in the pic.  There is a kind of distracting white string (?) to the right side of the photo on the table.  All for a small reflection on the shiny surface in the background, the lighting is great.  it is also a very nice drawing, which makes it visually interesting.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is very yellow.  I am sure you did it intentionally, so I''m going to leave it alone, however I might have either used b&w or plain old fashioned color.  You did a great job in creating the yellowness, just a bit too yellow for me.  Setting that aside, You have a great angle of the child and there is definately a pencil in the pic.  There is a kind of distracting white string (?) to the right side of the photo on the table.  All for a small reflection on the shiny surface in the background, the lighting is great.  it is also a very nice drawing, which makes it visually interesting.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-22 10:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107015, 4613, 2867, '<td valign="top">To me, the background pattern makes it look too cluttered and busy. I think that a plain background might look better in this picture.</td>', 'To me, the background pattern makes it look too cluttered and busy. I think that a plain background might look better in this picture.', '2002-08-22 15:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107016, 4613, 3087, '<td valign="top">I''m guessing he didn''t draw that interesting portrait, is it then a portrait of him? Nice shot, nice concentration on his face. Not sure what the white lines are at the right of the table? I do like this being BW but find the sepia/ yellow too strong for me.<br/>6, Kavey</td>', 'I''m guessing he didn''t draw that interesting portrait, is it then a portrait of him? Nice shot, nice concentration on his face. Not sure what the white lines are at the right of the table? I do like this being BW but find the sepia/ yellow too strong for me.6, Kavey', '2002-08-23 07:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107017, 4613, 1792, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, however black &amp; white or color might be more effective.</td>', 'Nice idea, however black & white or color might be more effective.', '2002-08-25 02:34:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107018, 4615, 1826, '<td valign="top">I really like the way you arranged the pencils, the fact that only one eraser is seen, and the backround color to set it all off. Nice job. :)</td>', 'I really like the way you arranged the pencils, the fact that only one eraser is seen, and the backround color to set it all off. Nice job. :)', '2002-08-19 06:39:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107019, 4615, 3127, '<td valign="top">Wonderful colors!</td>', 'Wonderful colors!', '2002-08-19 09:33:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107020, 4615, 1856, '<td valign="top">nice colors and composition.  like the punch of ''red'' with the top eraser.  Lisa</td>', 'nice colors and composition.  like the punch of ''red'' with the top eraser.  Lisa', '2002-08-19 11:40:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107021, 4615, 3080, '<td valign="top">Can''t figure out how photos are done, but I think I may see a hint of glue holding the pencils to the left together.  However, I''ve been wrong before.  I like this.  Great lighting, focus, and very creative.  Would love to see at what other angles you shot this. it could be open to SO many possibilities.  Great photo. Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Can''t figure out how photos are done, but I think I may see a hint of glue holding the pencils to the left together.  However, I''ve been wrong before.  I like this.  Great lighting, focus, and very creative.  Would love to see at what other angles you shot this. it could be open to SO many possibilities.  Great photo. Good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-19 13:31:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107022, 4615, 2000, '<td valign="top">Reminds me of an Escher painting I''ve seen.  Nice.</td>', 'Reminds me of an Escher painting I''ve seen.  Nice.', '2002-08-19 18:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107023, 4615, 2815, '<td valign="top">The color of this photo is fantastic!!! I really like it</td>', 'The color of this photo is fantastic!!! I really like it', '2002-08-19 18:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107024, 4615, 327, '<td valign="top">Fine job, good background, clear shot. Score 7 ~Kee</td>', 'Fine job, good background, clear shot. Score 7 ~Kee', '2002-08-19 19:38:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107025, 4615, 2172, '<td valign="top">Excellent!  I love the colors.  Very clean and sharp.  Also like the composition.  10!<br/>Ruthann</td>', 'Excellent!  I love the colors.  Very clean and sharp.  Also like the composition.  10!Ruthann', '2002-08-19 20:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107026, 4615, 656, '<td valign="top">good colours, lots of action</td>', 'good colours, lots of action', '2002-08-19 23:02:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107027, 4615, 2279, '<td valign="top">I really like the blue on orange with the little splash of eraser in the corner. :) 8.</td>', 'I really like the blue on orange with the little splash of eraser in the corner. :) 8.', '2002-08-20 01:18:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(107028, 4615, 2798, '<td valign="top">A good arrangement and framing with excellent use of colour. Nice even light.</td>', 'A good arrangement and framing with excellent use of colour. Nice even light.', '2002-08-20 08:46:00.000000', NULL, 1);
