(108505, 4724, 1128, '<td valign="top">Used to do this in High School (reminds me of the Aliens movie).  Terrific use of long exposure.  Very creative and difficult to pull off!</td>', 'Used to do this in High School (reminds me of the Aliens movie).  Terrific use of long exposure.  Very creative and difficult to pull off!', '2002-08-25 23:43:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(108506, 4724, 749, '<td valign="top">Wow, my previous best shot was of my right hand, and now my best shot is of my left hand! I must be onto something here ;o)<br/><br/>This shot, as per the details, was done using a very long shutter timing, and was lit solely by an anglepoise lamp reflected off a wall. The timings of the pencil movement took practice to get the right effect, and eventually I found that 3 seconds per ''hit'' for the first two and two seconds per hit for the other three worked about right - the dark background meant the pencil didnt need to be there as long as the ones with my arm behind.<br/><br/>Just for the record, I used the JMSetzler ''How did they do that'' thingy for his ''Quitting Time'' shot to work out how to get the effect, so my advice is for you to read them! :o) Other than that, thank''s for your comments and votes, and please PM me if you want further details...<br/><br/>- Manic -</td>', 'Wow, my previous best shot was of my right hand, and now my best shot is of my left hand! I must be onto something here ;o)This shot, as per the details, was done using a very long shutter timing, and was lit solely by an anglepoise lamp reflected off a wall. The timings of the pencil movement took practice to get the right effect, and eventually I found that 3 seconds per ''hit'' for the first two and two seconds per hit for the other three worked about right - the dark background meant the pencil didnt need to be there as long as the ones with my arm behind.Just for the record, I used the JMSetzler ''How did they do that'' thingy for his ''Quitting Time'' shot to work out how to get the effect, so my advice is for you to read them! :o) Other than that, thank''s for your comments and votes, and please PM me if you want further details...- Manic -', '2002-08-29 18:25:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(108507, 4726, 2140, '<td valign="top">loved the movie.<br/>how did you make the background so white?<br/>i like how the angle of the pencil and the square things contrast together. good work!</td>', 'loved the movie.how did you make the background so white?i like how the angle of the pencil and the square things contrast together. good work!', '2002-08-19 01:57:00.000000', NULL, 1),
