(108910, 4747, 1037, '<td valign="top">This is a great photo. I thought when this challenge topic came up that most of the photos would be studies of pencils or some other kind of static shot that doesn''t really express anything, and I was right! Your photo is a lot more engaging because it uses the pencil as a springboard to explore an emotion. The duotone is great, and I love the textures and shapes of the scrunched up paper :).</td>', 'This is a great photo. I thought when this challenge topic came up that most of the photos would be studies of pencils or some other kind of static shot that doesn''t really express anything, and I was right! Your photo is a lot more engaging because it uses the pencil as a springboard to explore an emotion. The duotone is great, and I love the textures and shapes of the scrunched up paper :).', '2002-08-21 11:25:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(108911, 4747, 772, '<td valign="top">I like the lighting and the tone and ''mood'' provided by this photo... the ''pencil'' presence is slightly weak though... Since the pencils exist in the shadows, I had to look for them and then determine if they were pencils or not :)  This is good work :) - 7 - jmsetzler</td>', 'I like the lighting and the tone and ''mood'' provided by this photo... the ''pencil'' presence is slightly weak though... Since the pencils exist in the shadows, I had to look for them and then determine if they were pencils or not :)  This is good work :) - 7 - jmsetzler', '2002-08-21 14:30:00.000000', NULL, 1),
