(109177, 4764, 3087, '<td valign="top">I find this photo a little crowded - I am not seeing the reasons behind the choices about what has been included in foreground and background. The immediate foreground being out of focus doesn''t appeal to me (I appreciate it may be intentional) and the pillows, white hat and magnets are distracting.<br/>I apologise if my comments are discouraging, and am happy to discuss them via PM if you would like to.<br/>Kavey</td>', 'I find this photo a little crowded - I am not seeing the reasons behind the choices about what has been included in foreground and background. The immediate foreground being out of focus doesn''t appeal to me (I appreciate it may be intentional) and the pillows, white hat and magnets are distracting.I apologise if my comments are discouraging, and am happy to discuss them via PM if you would like to.Kavey', '2002-08-20 07:32:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109178, 4764, 835, '<td valign="top">file looks too compressed and the majority of the picture is out of focus.  My eyes are drawn to twitty &amp; the cat but I can''t clearly see them.</td>', 'file looks too compressed and the majority of the picture is out of focus.  My eyes are drawn to twitty & the cat but I can''t clearly see them.', '2002-08-20 10:24:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109179, 4764, 2337, '<td valign="top">It looks like your focus was on the white (hat?) thing on the right hand side... There is alot of things here that I''m not sure if you wanted in the shot... For instance, did you mean to include the smoke detector in the upper right? or the chair, the speaker, etc?  Perhaps you could have made the subject clearer if you put a ''background'' behind your subject... Something as simple as a piece of construction paper, propped up behind the pencils could have improved the shot greatly... Always try to remember that the background is there... It was one of the hardest lessons for me...</td>', 'It looks like your focus was on the white (hat?) thing on the right hand side... There is alot of things here that I''m not sure if you wanted in the shot... For instance, did you mean to include the smoke detector in the upper right? or the chair, the speaker, etc?  Perhaps you could have made the subject clearer if you put a ''background'' behind your subject... Something as simple as a piece of construction paper, propped up behind the pencils could have improved the shot greatly... Always try to remember that the background is there... It was one of the hardest lessons for me...', '2002-08-20 16:44:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109180, 4764, 1005, '<td valign="top">Focus seems to be on the white hat.  I don''t care for your angle of attack, it''s too hard to see "what''s going on".  I don''t get the pencil coral or the stuff in the background.  Sorry, 5, Swash</td>', 'Focus seems to be on the white hat.  I don''t care for your angle of attack, it''s too hard to see "what''s going on".  I don''t get the pencil coral or the stuff in the background.  Sorry, 5, Swash', '2002-08-20 20:50:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109181, 4764, 1041, '<td valign="top">that looks painful!  there''s too much clutter in the background of this photo, i am especially intrigued by what you have framed there.  labels?  stickers? beer mats?  and why is the hardhat there? all that distracts from the actual subject -- gr8photos (3)</td>', 'that looks painful!  there''s too much clutter in the background of this photo, i am especially intrigued by what you have framed there.  labels?  stickers? beer mats?  and why is the hardhat there? all that distracts from the actual subject -- gr8photos (3)', '2002-08-21 16:41:00.000000', NULL, 1),
