(109265, 4768, 3189, '<td valign="top">Interesting way to look at things ... I like.</td>', 'Interesting way to look at things ... I like.', '2002-08-21 17:00:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109266, 4768, 82, '<td valign="top">Nicely framed, with good contrast.  I might increase the contrast a tad, but over all, very nice!  I like the variety of texture in the shavings vs. the smooth metal.</td>', 'Nicely framed, with good contrast.  I might increase the contrast a tad, but over all, very nice!  I like the variety of texture in the shavings vs. the smooth metal.', '2002-08-22 11:16:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109267, 4768, 3087, '<td valign="top">Takes me back in time. Great close up, nice composition, with some wonderful curves. Keeps my focus right inside the frame.<br/>7, Kavey</td>', 'Takes me back in time. Great close up, nice composition, with some wonderful curves. Keeps my focus right inside the frame.7, Kavey', '2002-08-23 08:04:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109268, 4768, 3279, '<td valign="top">Excellent stuff - the DOF really helps to focus the eye onto the pencil remains! One of my top pics for the week.</td>', 'Excellent stuff - the DOF really helps to focus the eye onto the pencil remains! One of my top pics for the week.', '2002-08-23 18:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109269, 4768, 3080, '<td valign="top">In regards to the title, I''d have to say Yes it is!  Almost did this one myself.  I would like to see the color version also to compare and find out why you went with b/w.  The angle is good and I like the placement in the frame.  Lighting is good.  The dark spot inside the pencil sharpener is a bit dark for my taste, but that''s just an opinion.  besides, it looks like it could have been a bit difficult to get light in there anyway.  I like how I can see all the way through the pencil sharpener.  I wonder how many people are going to knock this down for "not meeting the challenge?"  Personally, I say it meets the challenge right on.  Great job and good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'In regards to the title, I''d have to say Yes it is!  Almost did this one myself.  I would like to see the color version also to compare and find out why you went with b/w.  The angle is good and I like the placement in the frame.  Lighting is good.  The dark spot inside the pencil sharpener is a bit dark for my taste, but that''s just an opinion.  besides, it looks like it could have been a bit difficult to get light in there anyway.  I like how I can see all the way through the pencil sharpener.  I wonder how many people are going to knock this down for "not meeting the challenge?"  Personally, I say it meets the challenge right on.  Great job and good luck in the challenge.', '2002-08-24 11:14:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109270, 4768, 3500, '<td valign="top">Nice idea but it needs more contrast.</td>', 'Nice idea but it needs more contrast.', '2002-08-24 17:19:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109271, 4768, 637, '<td valign="top">nice use of b&amp;w; like that "boston" is inverted, and shavings are partially in shadow; also like use of dof; would like to see sharpener fill less of the frame and a more head-on perspective  5 sjgleah</td>', 'nice use of b&w; like that "boston" is inverted, and shavings are partially in shadow; also like use of dof; would like to see sharpener fill less of the frame and a more head-on perspective  5 sjgleah', '2002-08-25 11:21:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109272, 4768, 1042, '<td valign="top">I''ll bet you had a lot of comments asking where the pencil is. I think this is great....I love the idea. Could use a bit more focus and contrast for me...but I like it... 8</td>', 'I''ll bet you had a lot of comments asking where the pencil is. I think this is great....I love the idea. Could use a bit more focus and contrast for me...but I like it... 8', '2002-08-26 00:03:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(109273, 4768, 806, '<td valign="top">OH, rats! #62? Totally underrated! I love it!<br/></td>', 'OH, rats! #62? Totally underrated! I love it!', '2002-08-26 01:11:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(109274, 4768, 2427, '<td valign="top">I really got a kick out of this picture.<br/>Although it''s not a technically brilliant as many of the other submissions I''ve seen on this site, it captured the challenge for me w/o taking the middle of the road.<br/>It is one of the first planned, created photos I''ve done.<br/>For the most part in the past, I''ve taken pictures with ambient lighting and worked with whatever positioning there is.<br/>I know some didn''t care for the DOF or contrast, and these are things I''m working on.  I''m something of a purist in that I don''t ever really touch up the photo with the unsharp mask or re-crop.<br/>For these challenges I shoot in 640x480 and use the camera to crop.  It just feels more ''organic'' to me this way.</td>', 'I really got a kick out of this picture.Although it''s not a technically brilliant as many of the other submissions I''ve seen on this site, it captured the challenge for me w/o taking the middle of the road.It is one of the first planned, created photos I''ve done.For the most part in the past, I''ve taken pictures with ambient lighting and worked with whatever positioning there is.I know some didn''t care for the DOF or contrast, and these are things I''m working on.  I''m something of a purist in that I don''t ever really touch up the photo with the unsharp mask or re-crop.For these challenges I shoot in 640x480 and use the camera to crop.  It just feels more ''organic'' to me this way.', '2002-08-26 21:45:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(109275, 4769, 3084, '<td valign="top">Great image, a real standout effort.</td>', 'Great image, a real standout effort.', '2002-08-19 05:13:00.000000', NULL, 1),
